  "problem": "Find the coordinates of the center of mass of the plate.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $(\\overset{\u2015}{x},\\overset{\u2015}{y})=($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         \n$,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$",
  "worked_solution": "The center of mass of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overset{\u2015}{x},\\overset{\u2015}{y})=(\\frac{{M}_{y}}{M},\\frac{{M}_{x}}{M}),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $M={\u222c}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the mass of the lamina,\n\n- ${M}_{x}={\u222c}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\\,$ is the moment of the lamina about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- ${M}_{y}={\u222c}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis.\n\nIn part 1, we found that the mass of the plate is\n\n$$\nM=24.\n$$\n\nAlso, from parts 2 and 3, we know that \n\n$$\n{M}_{x}=36,\\,{M}_{y}=48.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\u2015}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{y}}{M}=\\frac{48}{24}=2,\\,\\,\\overset{\u2015}{y}=\\frac{{M}_{x}}{M}=\\frac{36}{24}=\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the center of mass of the lamina is $(2,\\frac{3}{2}).$",
